Subject: Return the folder of the running .nro as the base path on Switch
Upstream-base: fbe120f5020f8bdcb9cbf5ae28d9859b29781119

SDL2's Switch build has no base path, so SDL_GetBasePath returned NULL. The
program keeps its settings, saves, logs and disc image beside its .nro: take
that folder from the sdmc:/ path the Homebrew Menu passes as argv[0], and keep
SDL2's answer without one.

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 288cce3..a6c30f3 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -36,6 +36,9 @@ declared in `include/SDL3/s3_defs.h` and `include/SDL3_mixer/s3_mixer_defs.h` ex
   such as a Joy-Con pair split in two, is removed and added again. Power levels are unknown, and
   virtual joysticks, LEDs and sensors are not supported. `SDL_SendGamepadEffect` takes a libnx
   `HidVibrationValue`, which plays on each of the controller's actuators until the next rumble call.
+- On Switch, `SDL_GetBasePath` is the folder of the running `.nro`, taken from the `sdmc:/` path the
+  Homebrew Menu passes as `argv[0]`. Without such a path it is SDL2's answer, which on Switch is
+  none.
